+# XITA Direct-BLS delta v3.1.0 - correction r1
+
+**27 October 2026 - CONDITIONAL GO for restricted self-funded core transfers.**
+
+This is the corrected production-readiness report, not a new clean-slate audit and not an unrestricted sponsorship approval. It withdraws the blanket activation-related NO-GO rationale, incorporates the canonical public genesis, preserves the actual RPC evidence and distinguishes missing host attestation from an observed vulnerability.
+
+Read [report.pdf](report.pdf), [report.md](report.md), [launch-decision.md](launch-decision.md), [findings.csv](findings.csv), [verification.md](verification.md), [remediation.md](remediation.md) and [evidence/README.md](evidence/README.md). Integrity is recorded in [archive-manifest.json](archive-manifest.json); [evidence-public.zip](evidence-public.zip) contains the public-safe correction evidence.
+
+The prior 90-page draft and its proposed 337-file package were not merged and are not represented as fully archived by this correction publication. The [v3.0.0 predecessor](../2026-10-27-xita-direct-bls-final-v3.0.0/) remains unchanged. Historical traceability is explained in [prior-findings-matrix.md](prior-findings-matrix.md); historical-findings.csv preserves its original predecessor snapshot, not new r1 dispositions.
+
+The original independent Phase A master is unchanged and access-controlled. The public Phase A file is an explicitly labelled disclosure-safe summary, not a replacement hash preimage. No runtime code, node configuration, database or on-chain state is changed.
