+audit,id,original_severity,current_severity,disposition,title,original_condition,boundary_prerequisites,current_assessment,source_refs,corrections,tests,production,current_finding,duplicate_of,baseline_provenance
+2026-10-24,H-01,High,Medium,OPEN,External RPC source evidence and correlated-provider trust,"Common external RPC sources supplied signer source evidence, including XGR. Same-provider consistency checks and failover did not independently authenticate the provider view.","Control over source evidence consumed by enough otherwise honest signers; a malicious relayer alone is insufficient. Currently external evidence needs two matching operator-labelled complete witnesses, while native XGR uses locally committed state.","Each external witness is pinned to one endpoint for the complete receipt/route/FeeVault verification; exact block, transaction, log index, message, route and fee fields must match. One successful operator, duplicate labels or two disagreeing observations cannot reach the threshold. Any matching pair of distinct labels returns immediately. An earlier disagreement is not a global conflict veto and all configured providers need not be queried. Native XGR uses its synchronized local committed chain. L2 source evidence requires safe finality with numeric canonical hash equality and no latest fallback. Operator labels do not establish upstream independence. Two correlated matching views can affect every signer. This is not a provider-independent header/receipt inclusion proof; L2 safe is not final Ethereum settlement.","[""interchain/config.go:47-71"", ""interchain/evm/rpc_evidence_quorum.go:31-113"", ""interchain/runtime/iln_direct_signing.go:27-68"", ""interchain/runtime/iln_direct_signing.go:95-135"", ""interchain/evm/finality.go:17-62"", ""audits/H01_RPC_WITNESS_SECURITY_EVIDENCE.md""]","[{""repo"": ""xgr-network/xgr-node"", ""pr"": 58, ""merge_sha"": ""b2c3bb26b9efff774e9d16a91c212d71526b59e2"", ""scope"": ""Merged mitigation is present; correlated external-source trust remains""}, {""repo"": ""xgr-network/xgr-node"", ""pr"": 59, ""merge_sha"": ""39175b868dfd39da17be9d6a87de87273c6b85bf"", ""scope"": ""Merged mitigation is present; correlated external-source trust remains""}, {""repo"": ""xgr-network/xgr-node"", ""pr"": 62, ""merge_sha"": ""0184eaec64a4634c5604fa734652afe13cb8feb6"", ""scope"": ""Merged mitigation is present; correlated external-source trust remains""}]",TestIndependentSourceWitnessRequiresExactBlockAndReceipt PASS (Exact witness equality.); TestTwoIndependentOperatorsWithFailover PASS (Operator threshold and failover.); TestOneOperatorAndConflictingProvidersFailClosed PASS (One surviving operator and a conflicting pair reject; not evidence of a global conflict veto.); TestSafeFinalityNoFallbackToLatest PASS (Finality policy.); TestReceiptMustMatchFinalizedCanonicalBlockHash PASS (Canonical block binding.),Published v3.3.8 download digest and embedded VCS revision match the frozen source. Actual installed validator binary hashes remain unverified.,F-05,,Readable October24 PDF copy plus frozen public register; exact original PDF byte identity unverified.
+2026-10-24,M-01,Medium,Resolved original condition,VERIFIED,Gas sponsorship accepts source confirmations below the adopted native finality boundary,findWalletSourceTx accepted latest plus a confirmation depth without requiring the L2 safe head or matching the receipt block hash to the canonical block. checkCandidate reused that confirmed flag to authorize a company-funded gas grant.,"The optional sponsor is active and funded. An otherwise valid payer-bound paid source operation lies above the safe head or its receipt becomes orphaned. Route, fee, wallet and budget checks remain necessary. This concerns sponsor treasury exposure, not additional Direct-BLS mint authority.","The shared native-finality helper checks chain identity, requires the configured native head, pins that head by number/hash and compares the source receipt block hash. findWalletSourceTx returns a nonconfirmed state above that head, and sponsorOneCandidate refuses it before reservation or payment. The original latest=112/source=100/safe=64 condition and the orphaned receipt condition both fail closed in the actual current sponsor entrypoint.","[""apps/web/chain-finality.js:15-50"", ""apps/web/wallet-transfers.js:387-399"", ""services/managed-relay/gas-sponsor.mjs:100-116""]","[{""repo"": ""xgr-network/xgr-interchain"", ""pr"": 292, ""merge_sha"": ""31e5b4116ab58ccd96f78931d762219534401f9d"", ""merged_at"": ""2026-10-24T17:03:33Z"", ""scope"": ""Shared native-safe source and delivery verification. The source sponsorship portion closes M-01.""}]","Two targeted tests pass: the actual sponsor entrypoint rejects source block 100 above safe 64 before reservation/send, and rejects an orphaned receipt block hash before reservation/send. Synthetic RPC and sender fixtures; no live payout. 4/4 shared-finality tests pass, including unsupported safe signals, chain policy, canonical receipt comparison and pinned Mailbox-state observations. 23/23 wallet-transfer tests pass, reused from the lead auditor's run.",Current source and local failure-path behavior verified. Installed sponsor version and a real paid payout at the adopted source-finality boundary remain unverified.,,,Readable October24 PDF copy plus frozen public register; exact original PDF byte identity unverified.
+2026-10-24,M-02,Medium,Resolved original condition,VERIFIED,Provisional destination delivery becomes permanently completed indexed state,Mailbox state was read at latest despite a finality label; an initial true survived database refresh and wallet reconciliation after a canonical negative observation.,A provisional destination execution is reorganized or an RPC returns transiently inconsistent positive state; source transfer can remain valid.,"checkedDelivery now uses native-finality-qualified, block-pinned Mailbox state. Reconciliation revisits completed rows, persists block/hash and allows canonical false to overwrite true. The wallet accepts an independently qualified reversal. Queue starvation is separate N-11, not proof the old sticky-true condition remains.","[""services/indexer/transfer-index.mjs:63-72"", ""services/indexer/transfer-index-worker.mjs:197-225"", ""apps/web/verified-journey.js:94-121"", ""services/indexer/sql/010_native_delivery_finality.sql""]","[{""repo"": ""xgr-network/xgr-interchain"", ""pr"": 292, ""merge_sha"": ""31e5b4116ab58ccd96f78931d762219534401f9d""}]",Executed indexer M-02 finality-qualified false regression and browser verified-journey reversal regression; both passed. No real L2 reorganization.,Current source verified; backend deployment/database migration not independently attested. Live endpoint alone does not establish rollout.,,,Readable October24 PDF copy plus frozen public register; exact original PDF byte identity unverified.
+2026-10-24,M-03,Medium,Resolved original condition,FIXED_IN_CODE,On-demand Direct-BLS signing lacked synchronization protection,"Public/peer quorum hints could reach the common signer without the synchronization guard used by the periodic loop, allowing eligibility checks against stale local PoS state.",An unsynchronized node retains a route and locally active signer and receives an otherwise valid source-operation hint. Source evidence and destination set checks still applied.,"signDirectILNMessage checks IsSynchronized before evidence acquisition and immediately before SignByBLS. Automatic observation and public/peer hints converge on this signer; current-set and delivery checks precede signing. Existing tests cover signer activity/key binding, but no dedicated stale/lost-sync regression for all entry paths was found. Code correction is established, but targeted entry-path and lost-synchronization tests are needed for VERIFIED.","[""interchain/runtime/iln_direct_signing.go:92-135"", ""interchain/runtime/iln_quorum_request.go:195-210"", ""interchain/runtime/iln_quorum_request.go:211-238"", ""consensus/ibft/interchain_runtime.go:28-75""]","[{""repo"": ""xgr-network/xgr-node"", ""pr"": 58, ""merge_sha"": ""b2c3bb26b9efff774e9d16a91c212d71526b59e2"", ""scope"": ""Central early and immediate pre-signing synchronization checks""}, {""repo"": ""xgr-network/xgr-node"", ""pr"": 59, ""merge_sha"": ""39175b868dfd39da17be9d6a87de87273c6b85bf"", ""scope"": ""Central early and immediate pre-signing synchronization checks""}]",TestInterchainSignerEligibilityIsOptInActiveAndMatchingBLS PASS (Eligibility/key binding; not a direct synchronization regression.),Published v3.3.8 download digest and embedded VCS revision match the frozen source. Actual installed validator binary hashes remain unverified.,,,Readable October24 PDF copy plus frozen public register; exact original PDF byte identity unverified.
+2026-10-24,M-04,Medium,Medium,OPEN,Unbounded RPC can block failover and orderly worker shutdown,"In the original baseline, an established remote RPC call could wait indefinitely, including while a chain-selection mutex was held, preventing failover and orderly shutdown.",A stalled provider or network was sufficient; no flood was required.,"boundedILNRPC read/evidence calls use real context cancellation, twelve-second request/four-second dial timeouts and a response limit; Worker.Close cancels that shared context. SubmitMembership and SubmitILNGovernance select a verified URL, then create txrelayer.NewTxRelayer without injecting the bounded client or worker shutdown context. Both run preflight reads through relayer.Client and then SendTransaction. The node-owned txrelayer creates its own legacy jsonrpc.NewClient. The pinned ethgo HTTP transport constructs a fasthttp client without read/write deadlines and calls Do; those defaults are unlimited. Its Close method has no cancellation effect. WithReceiptTimeout changes the sleep between receipt polls, not the timeout of GetTransactionReceipt or any other HTTP call. These are reachable worker paths: governanceExecuteLoop synchronously calls executeGovernanceJob and is part of the WaitGroup; the main loop calls tick -> trySubmissions -> trySubmit -> SubmitMembership. Worker.Close waits for them; IBFT.Close invokes it before closing the syncer. Separately, chain-selection locks still span bounded provider I/O, finality polling can continue to five minutes after cancellation, and native receipt polling has a two-minute outer deadline without the worker shutdown context. Unbounded external submission/preflight I/O can still hold a worker and orderly shutdown despite read-side cancellation. Per-call or polling-loop limits on other clients do not impose deadlines on this separate transport. No live consensus stall is asserted. Current residual prerequisites: an authorized governance execution or eligible membership preflight/submission is active against an external chain and its separate legacy transport stalls. Actual consensus halt was not demonstrated.","[""interchain/evm/rpc_transport.go:23-125"", ""interchain/evm/rpc_failover.go:231-284"", ""interchain/runtime/worker.go:325-348"", ""interchain/evm/finality.go:64-86"", ""consensus/ibft/interchain_runtime.go:218-238"", ""interchain/runtime/governance_execute.go:24-47"", ""interchain/runtime/governance_execute.go:75-83"", ""interchain/evm/iln_governance_submit.go:130-153"", ""interchain/evm/client.go:400-448"", ""txrelayer/txrelayer.go:61-80"", ""txrelayer/txrelayer.go:95-135"", ""txrelayer/txrelayer.go:256-275"", ""interchain/runtime/worker.go:351-372"", ""interchain/runtime/worker.go:446-453"", ""interchain/runtime/worker.go:1070-1082"", ""interchain/runtime/worker.go:1168-1183"", ""consensus/ibft/ibft.go:688-700"", ""go.mod:60-63"", ""go.mod:240-243""]","[{""repo"": ""xgr-network/xgr-node"", ""pr"": 63, ""merge_sha"": ""fd39a0fb4d20163c6a6d93cb8cf5dc25f017f188"", ""scope"": ""PR63 corrects bounded read/evidence transport; external txrelayer submission/preflight remains outside that cancellation scope.""}]","TestILNRPCRequestCancellationOnWorkerShutdown PASS (Cancels only a boundedILNRPC parent context during mock HTTP I/O. Does not exercise txrelayer, external membership/governance submission, or complete Worker.Close.); TestILNRPCRejectsOversizedResponseAndMismatchedID PASS (Transport size and response-identity checks.)",Published v3.3.8 download digest and embedded VCS revision match the frozen source. Actual installed validator binary hashes remain unverified.,F-29,,Readable October24 PDF copy plus frozen public register; exact original PDF byte identity unverified.
+2026-10-24,M-05,Medium,Medium,OPEN,Interchain work is not completely bounded inside the validator process,"Per-message goroutines, expensive proof acquisition before authentication and governance proposals without total count/maximum future lifetime limits leave aggregate work and persistence unbounded.",An admitted peer submits syntactically acceptable frames. Proposals must satisfy current source/set checks. Interchain shares process and host resources with the regular validator.,"Direct checkpoint votes call full source verification before voter membership, eligibility and signature checks. Direct vote and quorum-hint work lacks comprehensive pre-I/O global/per-peer admission. Some other frame types are throttled. Gossip starts a goroutine per delivered message. Governance proposals reject expired payloads/duplicates but have no global count/disk or maximum-future-expiry bound before insertion/persistence. Response/connection/time limits and batching reduce cost without bounding total admitted work. Separation from synchronous IBFT verification hooks does not establish CPU, memory, RPC or disk isolation. No actual IBFT halt or invalid IBFT state was demonstrated.","[""network/gossip.go:108-122"", ""interchain/runtime/worker.go:830-880"", ""interchain/runtime/iln_checkpoint.go:167-201"", ""interchain/runtime/iln_quorum_request.go:211-238"", ""interchain/runtime/governance.go:201-240"", ""interchain/runtime/iln_storage.go:123-134"", ""interchain/evm/rpc_transport.go:27-58""]","[{""repo"": ""xgr-network/xgr-node"", ""pr"": 63, ""merge_sha"": ""fd39a0fb4d20163c6a6d93cb8cf5dc25f017f188"", ""scope"": ""Partial transport/batching/completed-quorum improvements; no complete aggregate admission fix""}, {""repo"": ""xgr-network/xgr-node"", ""pr"": 75, ""merge_sha"": ""9a00ff7d30c602e2eedb0b2ba3ff988c039f553c"", ""scope"": ""Partial transport/batching/completed-quorum improvements; no complete aggregate admission fix""}]","TestILNRPCRejectsOversizedResponseAndMismatchedID P