+2026-10-25,N-05,High,Resolved original circular stage dependency,VERIFIED,Two-hop sponsorship can deadlock before the final-destination gas grant exists,"The zero-native-balance two-hop journey required progress toward TX3 before a later grant became payable, while that progress itself required the destination gas whose grant had not yet been issued. The second-hop message/stage dependency created a circular liveness prerequisite.","A valid paid two-hop source quote promises gas, the wallet lacks the required downstream native gas, and the service follows its original stage-dependent grant schedule. No compromised actor is necessary.","All immutable positive quote grants are selected and authenticated from finalized TX1. The first-delivery, hub-onward and final-delivery stages do not require child operation records, TX2 delivery or TX3 execution. The normal wallet path requires confirmed upfront grants before TX2, while an exactly matched immutable zero-grant quote is allowed to continue without waiting for the sponsor.","[""services/managed-relay/gas-sponsor.mjs:25-40"", ""services/managed-relay/gas-sponsor.mjs:61-78"", ""services/managed-relay/gas-sponsor.mjs:100-134"", ""services/managed-relay/gas-sponsor.mjs:451-470"", ""apps/web/app.js:530-567"", ""apps/web/transfer-sponsor-evidence.js:6-25""]","[{""repo"": ""xgr-network/xgr-interchain"", ""pr"": 309, ""merge_sha"": ""ab6d98395824beb71733577b0f49b2d167ab2761"", ""merged_at"": ""2026-10-25T11:04:11Z"", ""scope"": ""Initial parent-authenticated final-delivery promise at continuation; later superseded by the fully upfront schedule.""}, {""repo"": ""xgr-network/xgr-interchain"", ""pr"": 311, ""merge_sha"": ""f65cdf89b55953778e2c5c6a50f341d22d3b7052"", ""merged_at"": ""2026-10-25T11:42:00Z"", ""scope"": ""All original signed grants become due immediately after independently verified TX1; wallet continuation gates on those grants.""}]","Executed the exact candidate SQL extracted from frozen runSponsorSweep against the actual PostgreSQL engine and current schemas. One paid two-hop parent with three immutable commitments and zero child operations yields all three grant stages immediately. Stage-eligibility, immutable quote binding, grant tampering and reserve-before-payment tests pass in the 92-test managed-relay suite. 3/3 wallet evidence tests pass: paid fees alone do not imply grants, positive promises remain gated, and only exact immutable zero-grant evidence permits ungated continuation.",No paid empty-gas one-hop or two-hop production journey was executed. Live sponsor availability was false. Source closure of N-05 therefore does not establish commercial end-to-end readiness.,,,Frozen public summary plus recovered final conversation dated2026-10-25T10:42:18Z; original35-page PDF and137-entry ZIP not recovered.
+2026-10-25,N-06,Medium,Medium,OPEN,Unpaid public quotes can consume the rolling daily sponsor budget,An unauthenticated public caller can obtain unused signed quotes whose positive gas commitments consume the finite sponsor budget even though no source fee is paid. Honest quotes then fail capacity admission.,"Sponsorship and positive quote issuance are enabled and sufficiently funded. Enough valid requests with native deficits are admitted to consume the available commitment budget; cheap replacement payer addresses and, if needed, multiple client IPs satisfy the bounded per-identity limits. The attacker does not need to broadcast TX1 or receive the gas grant.","The holding period is materially reduced, but the original public-reservation resource-exhaustion mechanism remains. Quote admission still records an unpaid positive promise and charges spentToday plus all unsettled promises to daily capacity. Request throttles allow four attempts per IP, two per payer and 120 globally per minute. The caller supplies a payer address without proving control or paying a reservation cost. Repeated admitted requests can keep a finite budget occupied; this is a conditional capacity attack, not a claim that every treasury or gas-price configuration is saturable from one IP.","[""services/managed-relay/server.mjs:339-360"", ""services/managed-relay/server.mjs:441-461"", ""services/managed-relay/tax-evidence.mjs:125-175"", ""services/managed-relay/sponsor-funding.mjs:42-52"", ""services/managed-relay/gas-sponsor.mjs:393-434"", ""services/managed-relay/sponsor-policy.mjs:11-13""]","[{""repo"": ""xgr-network/xgr-interchain"", ""pr"": 330, ""merge_sha"": ""54ec66f59070b342ba07d4d0a17a274ace5cc399"", ""merged_at"": ""2026-10-26T17:16:14Z"", ""scope"": ""Partial mitigation: release only expired unused quote liabilities after a finalized source nonce observation; executed or ambiguous obligations remain reserved.""}, {""repo"": ""xgr-network/xgr-interchain"", ""pr"": 331, ""merge_sha"": ""fdfd342671936fa7c74fc18be5e60ef8679f61c0"", ""merged_at"": ""2026-10-26T17:21:58Z"", ""scope"": ""Partial mitigation: lower the expiry selection grace from ten to five minutes; signed source execution lifetime remains 90 seconds.""}]","The rate-limiter test passes. The expiry regression checks the five-minute SQL threshold and confirms unavailable finality evidence causes no release. It does not simulate adversarial continuous quote saturation. A separate actual expiry-function test confirms one finalized-head response plus a number-tagged nonce call can append a resolution without an independent witness or post-call hash recheck. This is a separate trust/release caveat, not the unpaid-reservation DoS reproduction.","The deployed positive-quote permission path, treasury levels and achievable saturation rate were not measured. The read-only sponsor readiness state was already unavailable, so this audit cannot attribute live unavailability to N-06.",F-17,,Frozen public summary plus recovered final conversation dated2026-10-25T10:42:18Z; original35-page PDF and137-entry ZIP not recovered.
+2026-10-25,N-07,Medium,Resolved original aggregate-accounting condition,VERIFIED,Sponsor admission does not reserve aggregate spendable treasury against outstanding promises,"New signed quotes could each pass a per-quote or stale funding check without accounting for all outstanding promises, allowing aggregate signed obligations to exceed the spendable sponsor treasury.",Multiple valid sponsored quotes arrive while finite native funds are shared across their promised stages. Concurrent admission increases exposure; malicious private keys or principal-authentication bypass are unnecessary.,"Positive quote commitments are appended within one transaction after sorted per-chain advisory locks. Under each lock the code counts every unsettled promise except a proven expired-unused quote or a confirmed grant, reads current wallet balance and gas price, includes a bounded payout-gas reserve for every outstanding and new grant, and enforces both liquidity and daily capacity. Any failure rolls the whole quote transaction back before the HTTP response exposes its signature.","[""services/managed-relay/tax-evidence.mjs:118-180"", ""services/managed-relay/sponsor-funding.mjs:21-53"", ""services/managed-relay/server.mjs:453-463"", ""services/managed-relay/gas-sponsor.mjs:280-303""]","[{""repo"": ""xgr-network/xgr-interchain"", ""pr"": 330, ""merge_sha"": ""54ec66f59070b342ba07d4d0a17a274ace5cc399"", ""merged_at"": ""2026-10-26T17:16:14Z"", ""scope"": ""Aggregate outstanding-liability, fresh-funding and payout-gas accounting under the common per-chain advisory lock.""}]","Pure aggregate-capacity tests and actual saveQuoteEvidence calls with a fake pool verify rejection of insufficient funds/budget, one atomic commit for all grants, rollback and nonce/fee binding. These tests passed within 92/92 managed-relay tests. An actual PostgreSQL-engine run applied the exact migrations and exercised actual saveQuoteEvidence under the documented dedicated writer role. It exposed S-A01: the newly required operations-table SELECT is missing although health readiness checks pass; the permission failure rolls back all rows. This is a separate availability/permission integration defect, not permission to overcommit.","S-A01 blocks a documented dedicated-role installation until grants/readiness are corrected; a consolidated worker role may already possess the needed SELECT. The actual deployed role and live concurrency behavior were not inspected. VERIFIED is limited to original source-level accounting and executed local checks, not production reserve assurance.",,,Frozen public summary plus recovered final conversation dated2026-10-25T10:42:18Z; original35-page PDF and137-entry ZIP not recovered.
+2026-10-25,N-08,Medium,Resolved original premature-confirmation condition,VERIFIED,Outgoing gas-gift receipts can become permanently confirmed before the adopted native-chain finality threshold,"The worker could treat the first successful native-gift receipt as final and permanently close the one-shot grant, even while the payment remained above the adopted safe/committed native-chain threshold.","A sponsor payout is initially mined successfully, then reorganized or inconsistently reported before the adopted native finality threshold. The original durable confirmed state suppresses a legitimate later payment/recovery path.","Both immediate receipt handling and submitted-grant reconciliation invoke verifiedSponsorFinality before recording confirmed. The helper requires a successful matching receipt, a native head covering the receipt, matching canonical receipt block hashes and a freshly observed successful receipt. Base/Arbitrum use safe; XGRChain uses latest with two additional blocks. Unsupported or insufficient evidence retains submitted status and does not authorize duplicate payment.","[""services/managed-relay/gas-sponsor.mjs:136-158"", ""services/managed-relay/gas-sponsor.mjs:227-240"", ""services/managed-relay/gas-sponsor.mjs:340-360""]","[{""repo"": ""xgr-network/xgr-interchain"", ""pr"": 330, ""merge_sha"": ""54ec66f59070b342ba07d4d0a17a274ace5cc399"", ""merged_at"": ""2026-10-26T17:16:14Z"", ""scope"": ""Safe/canonical native payout confirmation used on the initial path and restart reconciliation.""}]",The actual finality-helper regression passes: Base receipt block 100 is held at safe 99 and accepted at safe 100; XGRChain requires latest at least 102 for block 100; unsupported safe RPC is held. The equality checks for canonical block and refreshed receipt hashes were additionally inspected in both call paths. No real reorganization or live payout was generated.,Runtime support for required tags was not established through a real outgoing gift. The installed worker and production recovery journal were not read; no RELEASED conclusion is warranted.,,,Frozen public summary plus recovered final conversation dated2026-10-25T10:42:18Z; original35-page PDF and137-entry ZIP not recovered.
+2026-10-25,N-09,Medium,Medium,OPEN,UI can present deferred native principal as completed payout without a claim action,"The native router deliberately treats a fully reserved deferred payout as successful message handling. Presentation equates final Mailbox handling with beneficiary balance receipt, and does not discover or expose the beneficiary-only withdrawal.",Authenticated inbound native XGR transfer to a recipient whose receive/fallback rejects or exceeds the bounded payout gas. No malicious BLS signer or transport replay is needed.,"The native router deliberately treats a fully reserved deferred payout as successful message handling. Presentation equates final Mailbox handling with beneficiary balance receipt, and does not discover or expose the beneficiary-only withdrawal. A user can see an apparently completed principal payout while value remains in router custody and requires a claim. A general smart wallet can call the claim function itself or direct payout to another address; a contract with no arbitrary-call or claim facility may be unable to recover. External ownership of a contract does not authorize an EOA to claim its balance.","[""contracts/XETAGuardedNativeWarpRouter.sol:12-38,68-85"", ""services/indexer/transfer-index.mjs:62-71,97-115"", ""services/indexer/transfer-index-store.mjs:47-57"", ""apps/web/transfer-status-flow.js:25-26,119-126"", ""apps/web/transfer-token-journey.js:10-19,63-85""]","[{""repo"": ""xgr-network/xgr-interchain"", ""pr"": 328, ""merge_sha"": ""dcf73448e0e190ade818c8c92de385323a3afeec"", ""scope"": ""Adds compact token journey labels; no claim-state recovery.""}, {""repo"": ""xgr-network/xgr-interchain"", ""pr"": 332, ""merge_sha"": ""4b8541b804a3e59608695ff371b54f86a1d22ba1"", ""scope"": ""Status/balance-refresh changes do not turn a reserved claim into principal receipt.""}, {""repo"": ""xgr-network/xgr-interchain"", ""pr"": 334, ""merge_sha"": ""b22e285a1fa8378bf14edc996b342dcaa15249a7"", ""scope"": ""Latest status modal refinements still mark the delivered path complete without pending-claim discovery.""}]","Real Mailbox and native router with explicitly mocked accepting ISM: delivered=true, recipient balance unchanged, claim fully backed, replay rejected, original beneficiary claims to alternate recipient, no residual debt. The actual UI projection reports: ""Transfer complete"", ""no further wallet action"", ""native unlock step complete"", and the summary ""XGR unlocked on XGRChain. Delivery verified."" These displayed claims do not establish beneficiary balance availability. No claim about a named third-party wallet's exact implementation; local composition is not a browser end-to-end or production transaction. BLS verification is mocked only for this payout test and covered separately in cryptographic tests.","Current deployed code and configuration are independently checked in this audit; no future deployment, real reorganization, production journal crash or compiler equivalence is implied.",F-09,,Frozen public summary plus recovered final conversation dated2026-10-25T10:42:18Z; original35-page PDF and137-entry ZIP not recovered.
+2026-10-25,N-10,Low,Resolved original condition with bounded local retention,VERIFIED,Known provisional source transfers disappear from displayed history after wallet reconnection,A wallet broadcast locator was lost on reconnect/reload before durable indexed discovery became available.,A broadcast has not yet been independently indexed; wallet/session reconnects.,"Public transaction hints are saved per wallet, restored on reconnect and shown separately from canonically verified pending journeys. Invalid/stale hints do not authorize actions. Retention is bounded to 32 hints and 365 days; cross-device recovery depends on canonical index or a known hash, not browser local storage.","[""apps/web/source-tx-hints.js:1-76"", ""apps/web/app.js:20,272,359-369"", ""apps/web/wallet-index-projection.js""]","[{""repo"": ""xgr-network/xgr-interchain"", ""pr"": 319, ""merge_sha"": ""b098e9eb54213fef16cdbd4e1ca711669185a567""}, {""repo"": ""xgr-network/xgr-interchain"", ""pr"": 321, ""merge_sha"": ""8af4ae639f5b75a69fbd823b0693cdcdd6ef1397""}]",source-tx-hints3/3; wallet projection5/5 and related pending/recovery tests passed. Browser smoke tests could not run without Chromium; no real wallet reconnect acceptance test.,Public app.js matches frozen source; all module/runtime combinations not attested.,,,Frozen public summary plus recovered final conversation dated2026-10-25T10:42:18Z; original35-page PDF and137-entry ZIP not recovered.
+2026-10-25,N-11,Medium,Medium,OPEN,Retired or unknown-route rows indefinitely starve delivery refresh,Rows lacking an active route occupy the oldest bounded delivery worklist and are skipped without changing their scheduling position.,"Sufficient historical retired/unknown-route rows remain at the front of the derived SQL worklist. This is a backlog condition, not arbitrary direct database access for public users.",PR310 explicitly remediates only wallet pagination. The independent refreshPendingDeliveries query still selects all routes before resolving them and immediately continues for unknown routes before its attempt timestamp update. A real PostgreSQL-engine run using current migrations reproduced repeated selection without any active-route RPC read. Wallet ordering and background delivery scheduling are separate paths.,"[""services/indexer/transfer-index-worker.mjs:197-225"", ""services/indexer/transfer-index-store.mjs:118-148""]","[{""repo"": ""xgr-network/xgr-interchain"", ""pr"": 310, ""merge_sha"": ""f353d540519da2a373cd31e86b9a61e1d01cdafb"", ""scope"": ""Partial: wallet API worklist only. PR body expressly says partial scope.""}]","Existing wallet query-order regression passed. New actual-SQL refresh starvation regression also passed by reproducing the still-open worker behavior (PGlite0.5.12, exact source schema/function). No production database access or concurrency stress.",No actual current retired backlog was inspected; live route index reports caught up.,F-26,,Frozen public summary plus recovered final conversation dated2026-10-25T10:42:18Z; original35-page PDF and137-entry ZIP not recovered.
+2026-10-25,N-12,Medium,Resolved original no-promise candidate poisoning condition,VERIFIED,Positive microfees make transfers without sponsorship promises eligible to starve owed grants,Older operations with any positive service fee could occupy the limited sponsor candidate worklist even though no immutable gas promise existed. Rejected no-promise rows stayed ahead of later payable grants and could repeatedly consume the candidate window.,Enough older valid positive-fee operations without gas commitments precede a genuine owed sponsored transfer. Creating those source operations can have a cost; arbitrary public writes to the database are not assumed.,The current candidate query inner-joins the exact payer/source/adapter/quote nonce/fee intent and its immutable commitment rows before ORDER BY and LIMIT 120. No-promise positive-fee transfers cannot consume that candidate window. Grant execution independently verifies the matching finalized source receipt and immutable promise.,"[""services/managed-relay/gas-sponsor.mjs:451-470"", ""services/managed-relay/gas-sponsor.mjs:61-78"", ""services/managed-relay/gas-sponsor.mjs:100-116""]","[{""repo"": ""xgr-network/xgr-interchain"", ""pr"": 311, ""merge_sha"": ""f65cdf89b55953778e2c5c6a50f341d22d3b7052"", ""merged_at"": ""2026-10-25T11:42:00Z"", ""scope"": ""The immutable-commitment-driven upfront selection also closes this original worklist-poisoning condition, though the PR title focuses on the commercial upfront flow. Attribution is based on the verified candidate-query diff.""}]","Applied the current schemas to the actual PostgreSQL engine, inserted 125 older positive-fee operations without promises and one later paid two-hop parent with three promises, and executed the exact frozen candidate SQL. All 125 no-promise operations are excluded; the only selected rows are final-delivery/arbitrum, first-delivery/xgrchain and hub-onward/xgrchain for the owed transfer.","The exact SQL behavior is locally verified, but no production workload, backlog or installed worker was inspected. This test is not a throughput or concurrent-session test.",,,Frozen public summary plus recovered final conversation dated2026-10-25T10:42:18Z; original35-page PDF and137-entry ZIP not recovered.
