+# Corrected launch decision - r1
+
+Audit: XITA-DBLS-2026-10-27-v3.1.0. Date: 27 October 2026.
+
+**CONDITIONAL GO for the restricted self-funded core transfer scope. Not an unrestricted GO; unattended sponsorship is not approved.**
+
+The activation-related blanket NO-GO rationale is withdrawn. Canonical genesis schedules securityAccounting at 12,186,213; retained rpc/rpc1 observations report v3.4.0 and 19 sampled block heights agree. F-01/F-02 are independently verified in the frozen source and included in the release. These corroborate deployment; they do not prove every installed host's binary or effective configuration.
+
+The conditions in report.md section 7 are mandatory: G1 corrected consensus code and canonical schedule; G2 assessed XGRChain/Base/Arbitrum route bindings and supported code-free native recipients; G3 no new sponsorship promises in this scope, with existing obligations preserved and controlled reconciliation; G4 bounded resource admission, recovery and backlog monitoring; G5 maintained committee, key custody, independent external witnesses and single active registry per chain.
+
+These are operational prerequisites, not a statement that all controls were independently inspected. No risk is accepted on behalf of the operator. Any contradictory activation evidence, accounting failure or new Critical/High principal-safety defect requires immediate reassessment. See report.md for owners, scope, evidence and triggers.
